<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jamaat al Muslimeen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jamaat al Muslimeen is a Muslim organisation in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad">Trinidad</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tobago">Tobago</a> led for decades by Yasin Abu Bakr. On 27 July 1990 about a hundred of its members stormed the parliament building and the state television station in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-of-spain">Port of Spain</a>, holding Prime Minister A. N. R. Robinson and other ministers hostage for six days. The coup attempt failed, and the hostage takers surrendered after an amnesty whose validity was later disputed in the courts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jamaat-al-muslimeen.jpg" alt="Jamaat al Muslimeen" width="320" height="312" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BaronJaguar · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Trinidad_and_Tobago_(2025).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
